      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code. what do i need to do to fix it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A Bosch dishwasher with an E15 error code is usually a sign of a water inlet valve issue, often caused by a clogged filter or a faulty valve, but before you reach for the tools, you should definitely check if your local water supply is actually flowing, because if the water pressure is too low, the machine might not be able to fill up properly, which is a common scenario for this specific error. To fix it, start by removing the bottom rack and checking the filter at the bottom of the tub for any debris, as a clogged filter can prevent water from entering the system, and if the filter is clean, you might need to inspect the water inlet valve itself for blockages or electrical faults, which is a more complex task that might require a multimeter or a replacement part. If you are not comfortable working with the electrical components inside the dishwasher, it is best to contact a professional technician, as they have the proper tools and experience to diagnose the issue accurately without causing further damage to the appliance.",
